      "text": "### Aerodynamic Flow Regimes"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-AERODYNAMICS.md#005",
      "path": [
        "01-AERODYNAMICS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:aeronautics:01-aerodynamics, git-history:aeronautics:01-aerodynamics]",
        "canonical_path": "aeronautics/01-AERODYNAMICS.md",
        "concepts": "[aerodynamics]",
        "current_path": "aeronautics/01-AERODYNAMICS.md",
        "id": "maxim:aeronautics:aerodynamics",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "aeronautics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[aerodynamics]",
        "section": "aeronautics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "01 - Aerodynamics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    AERODYNAMIC FLOW HIERARCHY                            │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                                                                          │\n│  GOVERNING EQUATIONS                                                     │\n│  Navier-Stokes: full viscous, compressible flow                         │\n│       │                                                                  │\n│       ├── High Re, inviscid: EULER EQUATIONS                            │\n│       │   → Potential flow, lifting line, panel methods                 │\n│       │                                                                  │\n│       └── Viscous region: BOUNDARY LAYER EQUATIONS (Prandtl)           │\n│           → Skin friction, separation, transition                        │\n│                                                                          │\n│  FLOW REGIMES by Mach:                                                  │\n│  M < 0.3: incompressible (ρ = const) — good for GA aircraft             │\n│  0.3 < M < 0.8: compressible subsonic — transonic corrections           │\n│  0.8 < M < 1.2: transonic — mixed regions, shock waves forming         │\n│  M > 1.2: supersonic — oblique shocks, expansion fans                  │\n│  M > 5: hypersonic — chemistry, ablation                               │\n│                                                                          │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```"
    },
