        "title": "01 - Aerodynamics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "### Potential Flow"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-AERODYNAMICS.md#015",
      "path": [
        "01-AERODYNAMICS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:aeronautics:01-aerodynamics, git-history:aeronautics:01-aerodynamics]",
        "canonical_path": "aeronautics/01-AERODYNAMICS.md",
        "concepts": "[aerodynamics]",
        "current_path": "aeronautics/01-AERODYNAMICS.md",
        "id": "maxim:aeronautics:aerodynamics",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "aeronautics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[aerodynamics]",
        "section": "aeronautics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "01 - Aerodynamics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**PDE bridge:** Potential flow solves Laplace's equation (nabla^2 phi = 0) — the same equation governing electrostatic potential and steady-state heat conduction. The full toolkit from complex analysis applies: analytic functions map conformally, and the Joukowski transform maps the solved cylinder+vortex problem to airfoil shapes. Thin airfoil theory replaces the airfoil with a singularity distribution on the chord line — a method-of-moments approach on Laplace's equation. This is why potential flow aerodynamics is a solved PDE problem, and why panel methods (discretized boundary integral equations) work so well."
    },
    {
      "id": "01-AERODYNAMICS.md#016",
      "path": [
        "01-AERODYNAMICS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:aeronautics:01-aerodynamics, git-history:aeronautics:01-aerodynamics]",
        "canonical_path": "aeronautics/01-AERODYNAMICS.md",
        "concepts": "[aerodynamics]",
        "current_path": "aeronautics/01-AERODYNAMICS.md",
        "id": "maxim:aeronautics:aerodynamics",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "aeronautics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[aerodynamics]",
        "section": "aeronautics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "01 - Aerodynamics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nIRROTATIONAL FLOW: ∇×**u** = 0 → exists velocity potential φ: **u** = ∇φ\n  Incompressible: ∇²φ = 0 (Laplace equation — same as electrostatics)\n  Superposition: sum of solutions is a solution"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-AERODYNAMICS.md#017",
      "path": [
        "01-AERODYNAMICS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:aeronautics:01-aerodynamics, git-history:aeronautics:01-aerodynamics]",
        "canonical_path": "aeronautics/01-AERODYNAMICS.md",
        "concepts": "[aerodynamics]",
        "current_path": "aeronautics/01-AERODYNAMICS.md",
        "id": "maxim:aeronautics:aerodynamics",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "aeronautics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[aerodynamics]",
        "section": "aeronautics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "01 - Aerodynamics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "ELEMENTARY FLOWS (building blocks):\n  Uniform flow: φ = U∞x (flow from left)\n  Source/sink: φ = (Q/2π)ln(r) (radial flow; Q = volume flow rate)\n  Doublet: source + sink at same point\n  Free vortex: φ = (Γ/2π)θ; ψ = −(Γ/2π)ln(r); circulation Γ"
    }
  ],
